To connect your local development environment to a Supabase database, you only need to change a few configuration details. Since I checked your backend/requirements.txt, I can see you already have psycopg2-binary installed, which means your project is perfectly ready to talk to a PostgreSQL database like Supabase!

Here are the exact steps to connect your project:

1. Get the Connection String from Supabase
Create a free account and a new project on Supabase.
Once the project is created, go to Project Settings (the gear icon) -> Database.
Scroll down to the Connection String section and select the URI tab.
Uncheck "Use connection pooling" for now (direct connection is better for local development and running initial migrations).
Copy the connection string. It will look something like this: postgresql://postgres.your_project_id:your_password@aws-0-region.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres
(Make sure you replace [YOUR-PASSWORD] with the actual database password you created).

2. Update your .env File
In your code editor, open the backend/.env file. You need to change the DATABASE_URL variable to use the Supabase connection string instead of your local SQLite database.

Change it from something like sqlite:///./sql_app.db to your copied string:

env
# In backend/.env
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres.your_project_id:your_password@aws-0-region.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"
3. Run Database Migrations
Since Supabase gives you a completely empty database, you need to tell your project to create all the LMS tables (Users, Courses, Assignments, etc.) inside Supabase.

Open your terminal, navigate to your backend folder, and run Alembic (your project's database migration tool):

bash
cd backend
# Make sure your virtual environment is activated
alembic upgrade head
If it succeeds, you will see Alembic create all the tables in your Supabase dashboard (under the "Table Editor" tab).

4. Run the Backend
Now, simply start your FastAPI server as usual:

bash
uvicorn app.main:app --reload
Your local backend is now fully connected to your live Supabase database! Any new users you register or assignments you create on localhost:5173 will be permanently saved in the Supabase cloud.

